---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
export const prerender = true;
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Legible Markets"
  description="What Legible Markets is, who it's for, and where the data comes from."
>
  <article class="about-root">
    <h1>About Legible Markets</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      DC isn't able to understand the information coming out of financial
      markets, except through specialized interpreters who often have their
      own agendas. Legible Markets aims to change that by enabling people to
      make dashboards of financial and economic information that they can
      share, remix, and understand.
      <a href={`${baseUrl}/compose/`}>Try it out</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>FRED</strong> (St. Louis Fed) — rates, inflation, employment, GDP, and most US-macro series.</li>
      <li><strong>Yahoo Finance</strong> (via <code>yfinance</code>) — equity tickers, ETFs, futures.</li>
      <li><strong>World Bank Open Data</strong> — country GDP shares.</li>
      <li><strong>EIA</strong> — retail fuel prices (where applicable). Each chart links to all data sources it uses.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      None of this is investment advice. Series can be revised, restated, or
      deprecated by their providers; the site reflects whatever was current on
      the most recent refresh.
    </p>

    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <p>
      Astro + TypeScript on the front end (Observable Plot for charts), Python
      pipelines for data, Vercel for hosting, Supabase (Postgres + Auth) for
      saved dashboards.
      <a href="https://github.com/khs/legible-markets" rel="noopener">Source on GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Built by</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://kellerscholl.com" rel="noopener">Keller Scholl</a>.
      Notes &amp; corrections welcome at
      <a href="mailto:keller.scholl@gmail.com">keller.scholl@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Legal disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Not investment advice.</strong> Everything on this site is
      published for informational and educational purposes only. Nothing here
      is investment, financial, tax, legal, or trading advice, and nothing
      should be construed as a recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any
      security or other financial instrument. Market and economic data can
      be revised, delayed, restated, or simply wrong; reflected values are
      whatever the upstream provider returned at the most recent data refresh
      and may not be current. Do your own research, and consult a qualified
      professional before making any financial decision. The site, its data
      providers, and its author make no warranties of accuracy, completeness,
      timeliness, or fitness for any particular purpose, and accept no
      liability for losses arising from use of this information.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Privacy &amp; analytics.</strong> The site uses Vercel Web
      Analytics to count visits and key product events (e.g. "a chart was
      added", "a save was attempted"). Vercel's analytics is cookieless and
      does not collect personally identifiable information &mdash; no IP
      addresses are stored, no fingerprinting is performed, and no third-party
      ad tracking happens on this site. If you create an account, your
      Google-provided email is stored in our Supabase database solely so we
      can attach your saved dashboards to you; we don't sell, share, or
      market against this information. You can delete your account and all
      associated saves at any time by emailing
      <a href="mailto:keller.scholl@gmail.com">keller.scholl@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Data licensing.</strong> Underlying series carry their providers'
      licensing terms: FRED data is U.S. public domain; World Bank Open Data
      is CC BY-4.0; Yahoo Finance and EIA data are used under each
      provider's published terms of service. Charts and dashboards composed
      from these sources inherit those terms; please credit the underlying
      provider when reproducing data elsewhere.
    </p>

    <p class="footer-note">
      <a href={baseUrl || "/"}>&larr; All dashboards</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-root {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 24px 80px;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .about-root h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .about-root h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
    color: var(--color-neutral-900);
  }
  .about-root p,
  .about-root ul {
    margin: 8px 0;
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
  }
  .about-root ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .about-root li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .about-root .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-neutral-800);
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .about-root code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  .about-root a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .footer-note {
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(55, 53, 47, 0.08);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
